# Mee Myself and I — C-Mee-PO

When drafting or editing `mee-myself-and-i` Guide posts, follow the full charter in `utilities/penang-pulse/EDITORIAL.md` → **Mee Myself and I — C-Mee-PO voice** and **Guides publish cycle (learnings)**.

## Hard rules

- Human narrator = venue, timing, taste, judgment. **C-Mee-PO** = dish/ingredient lore (reused research OK).
- Attribute with `**C-Mee-PO:**` in normal body paragraphs after a short prose setup.
- When he asks a question, keep `**C-Mee-PO:**` on that line; answer in plain first person (no `Me:`).
- Optional once-per-article `###` for a long brief only.
- Never put C-Mee-PO in `>` — that renders as a practical tip. Reserve `>` for cash/queue/caveats.
- Catchphrases: ~1 per article. Singularity dinner line only for heavy/fatty/spicy, max every 4th–5th episode.
- CMS Build ≠ live. Publish via Firebase: `npx firebase-tools deploy --only hosting:penang-pulse` → verify `https://penangpulse.com`.

## Pattern

```markdown
I asked C-Mee-PO what I was actually eating.

**C-Mee-PO:** [research summary]

I’d eat that if I had a mouth!
```
